35,2,1,talk,May,,"The pilots from eight years ago actually worked. The ferry contactless trial closed clean, and the late-evening timetable hit its cost target.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, that’s good news, but my rosters are bleeding. The late-turn pool is down to a skeleton crew, and overtime is eating the budget.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, that explains the waiting. My audits show the minutes are lost in the gaps, not the queues. The platforms aren’t the problem.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, I see the pattern. The accessibility lifts finished on time, but the lane-priority stretches were pulled back. The ground hides the delays.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I found the real leak. The ticketing contractor fees are now higher than our paving budget, and the capital ledger is still tied up in a lapsed grant.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, if the ledger is tied up, we can’t fund the pilots again. We need to know what’s actually free.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, the maintenance contract has spare capacity for the lifts, but the roadway crews are a third below establishment. We can’t run more trains without more hands.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, then the fix isn’t more platforms. It’s tighter connections. My timed runs show the surface route is the bottleneck, not the stations.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, I agree. The committee minutes show the ferry and rail offices never agreed on data terms. That’s the real stall.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, that’s the trap. If we don’t fix the data terms, the next plan is just another promise we can’t keep.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,"So the pilots prove the tech works, but the staffing and data terms are the real walls. We need a plan that respects both.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Exactly. A plan that asks for more crews is a plan that will fail. We need to work with what we have, or find the spare capacity.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"A plan that fixes the connections, not the crowds. The data is clear. The waiting is the cost, not the standing.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shizue,,A plan that gets the ferry and rail offices to sign the same paper. That’s the only way to stop the stalls.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,A plan that doesn’t add a single new liability. The ledger is full. The fees are high. We have to be careful.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,May,,"I’m leaning toward the plan that uses the existing pilots. It’s proven, and it doesn’t ask for more money.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I’m leaning toward the plan that uses the spare maintenance capacity. It’s the only one that doesn’t break the rosters.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,I’m leaning toward the plan that fixes the connections. It’s the only one that matches the data.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I’m leaning toward the plan that gets the data terms signed. It’s the only one that will actually deliver.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I’m leaning toward the plan that doesn’t add new fees. It’s the only one that won’t break the ledger.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
